    <item>
      <title>Pyenv in WSL</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/python/pyenv/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 28 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/python/pyenv/</guid>
      
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;setting-up-pyenv-in-wsl-ubuntu&#34;&gt;Setting Up &lt;code&gt;pyenv&lt;/code&gt; in WSL (Ubuntu)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;pyenv&lt;/code&gt; is a tool that allows you to manage multiple Python versions easily. This guide will walk you through setting up &lt;code&gt;pyenv&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;strong&gt;WSL Ubuntu&lt;/strong&gt; and installing Python &lt;strong&gt;3.11&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=&#34;pyenv.webp&#34; alt=&#34;pyenv image&#34; style=&#34;width:60%; height:auto;&#34;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;step-1-update-and-install-dependencies&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 1: Update and Install Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before installing &lt;code&gt;pyenv&lt;/code&gt;, update your system and install necessary build dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sh&#34; data-lang=&#34;sh&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo apt update &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; sudo apt upgrade -y
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo apt install -y make build-essential libssl-dev zlib1g-dev &lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    libbz2-dev libreadline-dev libsqlite3-dev curl &lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    libncursesw5-dev xz-utils tk-dev libxml2-dev &lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;se&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    libxmlsec1-dev libffi-dev liblzma-dev
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pr</description>
      
